    {
      "title": "Split at zero",
      "body": "<p>For negative <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>. For nonnegative <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>.</p>",
      "recap": "The modulus sign must be removed differently on the two sides of zero.",
      "pitfall": "Only <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> is inside the modulus; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> keeps its own sign.",
      "pause": "Write the two integrals without modulus signs.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l21",
          "reminder": "The modulus sign must be removed differently on the two sides of zero."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Integrate each part",
      "body": "<p>Expand the expression inside each integral and integrate the powers of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>. Evaluate each part between its own limits, then add.</p>",
      "recap": "For each definite integral, subtract the value at the lower limit from the value at the upper limit.",
      "pitfall": "Keep negative contributions; this question asks for the integral, not the unsigned area.",
      "pause": "Calculate both parts and simplify their sum.",
      "recall": [
